# Import of the MelodyHPO working tree (2.2 GB on disk, ~99% of it virtualenvs
# and tool caches). Only the `dataseq` ancestry is wanted on this branch, so the
# rule is deny-by-default: nothing here is tracked unless it is named below.
#
# This file lives in `.scratch/dl/` rather than the repo root so that each import
# owns its own rules -- see `.scratch/README.md`. (It originally said "so that
# deleting `.scratch/` at the end of the merge removes the rules along with what
# they describe". `.scratch/` is no longer deleted, as of 2026-08-31: it is the
# migration source for `hmm` and `align` 0.1.0 too. Per-import locality still
# holds, and now earns its place differently -- the tracked set is re-scoped per
# package, and a policy that lives beside what it governs can be narrowed without
# touching the other three.)
#
# The repo-root `.gitignore` still applies underneath these rules, and is what
# keeps `.env`, `.DS_Store`, `__pycache__/`, `.venv*`, and the mypy/ruff/pytest
# caches out even inside the re-included directories. Do not restate those here;
# a negation added below could re-admit them by accident.

# --- deny everything at this level -------------------------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore
!/MelodyHPO/

# Our own writing about the import -- ANALYSIS.md and anything joining it. This
# negation is easy to forget and fails silently: a file written here without it
# is simply invisible to `git status`, so the work looks committed and is not.
!/*.md

# --- deny everything one level in, then name the exceptions ------------------
/MelodyHPO/*

# The merge base itself. `melody_hpo/data/` is the code this branch exists to
# merge; the rest of the package is here because the container and the encoder
# are only legible against the model and training code that consume them.
!/MelodyHPO/melody_hpo/

# Curated dataset assembly -- document collections, splits. Version-controlled
# upstream, and the closest thing MelodyHPO has to a spec for what a "dataset"
# is expected to look like coming out of the container.
!/MelodyHPO/minicorps/

# Tests are evidence of intended behaviour, and the merged container has to keep
# passing whatever they assert about the encoder's contract.
!/MelodyHPO/tests/

# Declared runtime dependencies. `docs/plan/DEFERRED.md` makes `dataseq`'s own
# third-party dependencies a function of what the merge base actually needs, and
# this file is that evidence.
!/MelodyHPO/pyproject.toml

# Narrative context for reading the above.
!/MelodyHPO/README.md
!/MelodyHPO/ARCHITECTURE_REFERENCE.md

# --- deliberately not tracked, with reasons ----------------------------------
# Named here rather than left to the catch-all so that the reasoning survives.
#
#   data/            5.4 MB of ingested CSVs. Gitignored in MelodyHPO too, and
#                    it is a checkout of a *separate* repo (MelodyData), not
#                    MelodyHPO's own content. Readable on disk; not ours to
#                    vendor. Provenance is recorded in `.scratch/README.md`.
#   LLMsFS/          12 MB vendored clone of an unrelated book repo.
#   notebooks/       Exploratory, and diffs badly.
#   uv.lock          292 KB resolved for a project we are not building.
#   CLAUDE.md.orig,  Agent instructions for a different project. Renamed on import
#   PROJECT_...md,   -- Claude Code loads a nested CLAUDE.md when reading files
#   TODO.md          beside it, so under its original name this file would inject
#                    MelodyHPO's rules into a pfsmgraph session regardless of
#                    whether it is tracked. See `.scratch/README.md`.
#   configs/,        Empty upstream.
#   experiments/
